course: dictionary
lesson: 4316
title: Groundhog and Groundhog Day
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can tell you its meaning through the words around it. Look at this: «Alpine marmots are big ground squirrels that whistle to warn each other of eagles and foxes and hibernate for about six months in family groups; the American groundhog is a marmot too.» The clues are ground squirrels and hibernate, so a groundhog must be a similar animal that lives in the ground.
explain: «On Groundhog Day in America people pretend a groundhog predicts when spring will come, but no animal can really forecast the weather weeks ahead.» The words pretend and but warn you that this is a made-up custom, not real science. Always ask: does this sentence sound like a fact or a game?
explain: Sometimes a word has a special meaning in everyday talk. If someone says, «Every Monday at school feels like Groundhog Day», they mean the same boring thing keeps happening again and again. Try the meaning in the sentence: does it still make sense? If yes, you have got it.
fact: A groundhog is a large brown rodent from North America, also called a woodchuck.
fact: A groundhog lives in a burrow and sleeps through the winter.
fact: Groundhog Day is a custom in the USA and Canada: if the groundhog sees its shadow, there will be six more weeks of winter.
fact: Groundhog Day is folklore, not science: no animal can really forecast the weather weeks ahead.
fact: Informally, «Groundhog Day» means a situation that keeps repeating in the same boring way, from a famous film.
exercise: What is a groundhog? | A flower that grows in the desert | *A large brown rodent from North America that lives in burrows | A fish that swims in rivers | A bird that sings at dawn
exercise: «On Groundhog Day in America people pretend a groundhog predicts when spring will come.» What does pretend mean here? | Tell the exact truth about | Dig a deep hole | Run very fast | *Act as if something is true when it is not
exercise: Your big sister says, «Another day of cleaning my room. It's like Groundhog Day!» What does she mean? | *The same boring thing keeps happening again and again | It is a special holiday with presents | It is going to snow for six weeks | Someone has found a real groundhog
test: What does a groundhog do in winter? | Flies south to warmer lands | Builds a nest high in trees | Sings loudly every night | *Sleeps through it in its burrow
test: Why is Groundhog Day not a real forecast? | The shadow always shows that spring is coming | *It is folklore, and no animal can really forecast the weather weeks ahead | It is proven by careful science every single year | Groundhogs only come out at night
exam: Which word is another name for a groundhog? | Hedgehog | Fox | *Woodchuck | Eagle
